  "narration": {
    "transcript": "From a storyboard to the screen. Here is how we built a whiteboard video engine. It starts with one file: plain text in, a finished video out. One hand, one marker, and the nib follows every stroke. Real handwriting, brushed on stroke by stroke. A growing library of drawn doodles, your own illustrations, and flip-book animations. It colours things in. It is proven: silent or narrated, vertical or widescreen, ninety-seven automated tests, zero pen collisions. Storyboard in, video out. Even this one."
  },
